==Battleground==
*1 [[Brollow]] spawns after 3.33 seconds<sup>100f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**30 [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 0.67~2 seconds<sup>20f~60f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Brollow]]s spawn, delay 6.67~10 seconds<sup>200f~300f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use 4 meatshields and [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] if you have them and the stage will be much easier! [[Kotatsu Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Kotatsu Cat]] and [[Titan Cat (Normal Cat)|Jamiera Cat]] are very useful for this stage as they can take many hits from the Brollows. [[Ururun Wolf (Special Cat)|Ururun]]'s good range and attack rate are perfectly suited to the Brollow hordes, but be careful not to let them clip into her. At high levels, [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]] can be spammed to do massive damage to the Brollows without them starting to plow through your meatshields.

If you have [[Sardine (Special Cat)|Sardine]]/[[Miku Cat (Rare Cat)|Miku Cat]]/[[Ranma Cat (M) (Rare Cat)|Ranma Cat]], they will be a great luck-reliant second layer of meatshields; Depending on your own luck, they could save you by activating their Dodge, but do not rely on it.

If you have [[Warlock and Pierre (Uber Rare Cat)|Warlock and Pierre]] at level 20, you can [[cheese]] this stage by using them. Since the base has 300,000 HP and there's no boss in this stage, Warlock and Pierre can instantly destroy the enemy base and you won't have to face the flock of Brollows.

